  "did_you_know": "The monstrous chimaera adds a goat head and snake-headed tail to the already fearsome lion.",
  "early_education_description": null,
  "artlens_description": null,
  "description": "The lion, king of the beasts and an animal associated with regal and heroic power, featured prominently on the coinage of many ancient Greek city-states. Artists placed the lion in a variety of poses, sometimes including the whole body, at other times the foreparts or just the head. Although it may once have roamed nearby, for many Greeks the lion was a monster nearly as exotic as the Chimaera, of which it formed a part (together with a goat head and snake-headed tail, as seen on this Sikyonian coin).",
